  html: "<h2 class=\"text-[12pt] text-orange-300 mb-8 font-light tracking-wide\">Belgian data retention framework under Article 15(1) ePrivacy Directive (post-La Quadrature du Net II)</h2>\n<table class=\"w-full mb-6 border-collapse border border-red-900/30\"><thead><tr><th class=\"px-3 py-2 text-left text-red-400 border-b border-red-900/50 text-xs font-bold tracking-wider\">Field</th><th class=\"px-3 py-2 text-left text-red-400 border-b border-red-900/50 text-xs font-bold tracking-wider\">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-[#39ff14] text-xs border-b border-red-900/20\"><strong class=\"text-orange-300 font-bold\">Location</strong></td><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-[#39ff14] text-xs border-b border-red-900/20\">Belgium</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-[#39ff14] text-xs border-b border-red-900/20\"><strong class=\"text-orange-300 font-bold\">Jurisdiction</strong></td><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-[#39ff14] text-xs border-b border-red-900/20\">National</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-[#39ff14] text-xs border-b border-red-900/20\"><strong class=\"text-orange-300 font-bold\">Status</strong></td><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-[#39ff14] text-xs border-b border-red-900/20\">ACTIVE</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-[#39ff14] text-xs border-b border-red-900/20\"><strong class=\"text-orange-300 font-bold\">Severity</strong></td><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-[#39ff14] text-xs border-b border-red-900/20\">4/5 — HIGH</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-[#39ff14] text-xs border-b border-red-900/20\"><strong class=\"text-orange-300 font-bold\">Categories</strong></td><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-[#39ff14] text-xs border-b border-red-900/20\">data_retention, traffic_retention</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2 class=\"text-[12pt] text-orange-300 mb-8 font-light tracking-wide\">Description</h2>\n<p class=\"mb-6 text-[#39ff14] leading-relaxed max-w-3xl\">Belgium implements data retention using CJEU &#39;targeted retention&#39; exception where the &#39;specific, crime-affected area&#39; has the same borders as Belgian state territory - effectively general retention.</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-[12pt] text-orange-300 mb-8 font-light tracking-wide\">Severity Rationale</h2>\n<blockquote class=\"border-l-2 border-orange-500/50 pl-4 mb-6 text-orange-400/70 italic\"><p class=\"mb-6 text-[#39ff14] leading-relaxed max-w-3xl\">Universal application (entire territory as &#39;targeted area&#39;) [+1], no judicial oversight for retention [+1], irreversible data collection (metadata databases) [+1], mission creep using CJEU &#39;targeted retention&#39; exception [+1], digital exclusion not applicable [0]. Total: 4/5</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2 class=\"text-[12pt] text-orange-300 mb-8 font-light tracking-wide\">Implementation Notes</h2>\n<p class=\"mb-6 text-[#39ff14] leading-relaxed max-w-3xl\">EXPLOITING CJEU LOOPHOLE FOR MASS SURVEILLANCE. Legal basis: Article 15(1) ePrivacy Directive allows targeted retention in &#39;specific, particularly crime-prone areas.&#39; Belgian implementation: The &#39;specific area&#39; = entire Belgian territory. This follows CJEU La Quadrature du Net II (2024) ruling that allowed targeted retention without national security threat. CJEU also permitted universal IP address retention for serious crime. Belgium&#39;s approach: Creative interpretation of &#39;targeted&#39; to mean &#39;national.&#39; Similar to France&#39;s rotating short-term retention claiming continuous national security threat. Concerns: (1) Circumvents CJEU Digital Rights Ireland ruling against general retention; (2) No transparency about what data retained, for how long; (3) Law enforcement access procedures unclear; (4) Creates surveillance infrastructure for social control. Opposition: EDRi and digital rights groups criticizing &#39;creative&#39; interpretations of CJEU exceptions. Verfassungsblog analysis documents exploitation of loopholes. Workers&#39; concern: Mass surveillance of communications metadata enables mapping of worker networks, union organizing, protest planning. Location data particularly sensitive for tracking worker movements.</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-[12pt] text-orange-300 mb-8 font-light tracking-wide\">Sources</h2>\n<ul class=\"mb-6 space-y-2 list-none pl-0\"><li class=\"flex items-start gap-2 text-[#39ff14]\"><span class=\"text-red-400 mt-1 shrink-0\">&#9658;</span><span><strong class=\"text-orange-300 font-bold\">[CIVIL_SOCIETY]</strong> <a href=\"https://verfassungsblog.de/data-retention/\" class=\"text-orange-400 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-orange-200\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Verfassungsblog - Analysis of Belgian data retention exploiting CJEU exceptions</a></span></li>\n<li class=\"flex items-start gap-2 text-[#39ff14]\"><span class=\"text-red-400 mt-1 shrink-0\">&#9658;</span><span><strong class=\"text-orange-300 font-bold\">[NEWS]</strong> <a href=\"https://www.loyensloeff.com/the-legal-500-country-comparative-guides---belgium---data-protection-and-cybersecurity---2024.pdf\" class=\"text-orange-400 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-orange-200\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Loyens &amp; Loeff - Belgium data protection and retention overview 2024</a></span></li>\n<li class=\"flex items-start gap-2 text-[#39ff14]\"><span class=\"text-red-400 mt-1 shrink-0\">&#9658;</span><span><strong class=\"text-orange-300 font-bold\">[PRIMARY]</strong> <a href=\"https://curia.europa.eu/juris/document/document.jsf?text=&amp;docid=281316&amp;pageIndex=0&amp;doclang=EN&amp;mode=req&amp;dir=&amp;occ=first&amp;part=1&amp;cid=6413403\" class=\"text-orange-400 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-orange-200\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CJEU La Quadrature du Net II judgment (C-470/21) on data retention</a></span></li>\n</ul>\n<hr class=\"border-red-900/40 my-6\" />\n<blockquote class=\"border-l-2 border-orange-500/50 pl-4 mb-6 text-orange-400/70 italic\"><p class=\"mb-6 text-[#39ff14] leading-relaxed max-w-3xl\"><strong class=\"text-orange-300 font-bold\">Source:</strong> @grey-c0 / Navigators Guild<br>Retrieved via <a href=\"https://github.com/grey-c0/legislation\" class=\"text-orange-400 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-orange-200\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">grey-c0/legislation</a><br>Integrated into scale_9.4 CAS pipeline — do not edit stubs manually.</p>\n</blockquote>\n",
